1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,210
This year's ozone hole was the biggest in a decade.

2
00:00:03,717 --> 00:00:04,888
On November fourth,

3
00:00:04,888 --> 00:00:09,758
NASA and NOAA reported it averaged about twenty-five million square kilometers.

4
00:00:09,758 --> 00:00:11,731
About the size of North America.

5
00:00:12,217 --> 00:00:15,094
The cause was an unusually strong polar vortex.

6
00:00:15,094 --> 00:00:16,196
And the good news?

7
00:00:16,196 --> 00:00:17,849
The layer is still healing.

8
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,427
So what if the ozone layer disappeared?

9
00:00:20,727 --> 00:00:22,975
Like and subscribe for more Earth what-ifs.

10
00:00:23,275 --> 00:00:25,547
Squeeze all that ozone down to sea level,

11
00:00:25,547 --> 00:00:27,985
and it's only about three millimeters thick.

12
00:00:28,483 --> 00:00:32,961
That thin shield soaks up all of the Sun's UV-C, and most of its UV-B.

13
00:00:32,961 --> 00:00:37,696
In a NASA simulation of a world that never banned ozone-killing chemicals,

14
00:00:37,696 --> 00:00:40,638
you could get sunburned in about five minutes.

15
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,560
What does space radiation do to your body?

16
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,052
Full story on the channel.
